<section class="hero container detail-hero"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Serga Revenue</p><h1>Know what you’ve sold.<br /><em>What happens next.<br />And what it’s worth.</em></h1><p class="hero-description">Subscription &amp; recurring revenue management for the products and services you sell to customers.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button button-dark" href="/contact">Book a demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/platform">Explore the platform <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>

<section class="container revenue-showcase"><partial name="_RevenueMockup" /><partial name="_RevenueBreakdowns" /></section>

<section class="detail-section container"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">The commercial truth between systems</p><h2>A won deal.<br /><em>An ongoing relationship.</em></h2><p>A deal closes in CRM. Invoices eventually appear in ERP. The products, quantities, prices and renewal commitments in between too often live in spreadsheets, work management tools and individual knowledge.</p></div><div class="capability-grid"><article><h3>What was sold</h3><p>Customers, products, configurations, plans, licenses and quantities — with subscription start and end dates.</p></article><article><h3>On what terms</h3><p>Pricing, currency, notice periods, renewals, price adjustments, indexation and invoice schedules.</p></article><article><h3>What it’s worth</h3><p>Annual recurring revenue (ARR), monthly recurring revenue (MRR), upcoming renewals, expansion and contraction.</p></article></div></section>

<section class="detail-section container"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">An annual software relationship</p><h2>Beyond the sale.<br /><em>Through every renewal.</em></h2><p>A software provider can manage annual licenses, maintenance and support with Serga Revenue alone. No Serga Service needs to exist.</p></div><ol class="workflow"><li><span class="eyebrow">01</span><strong>Won business</strong><p>Bring the customer and agreed product configuration into commercial context.</p></li><li><span class="eyebrow">02</span><strong>Subscription terms</strong><p>Connect licenses, quantities, price, currency and dates.</p></li><li><span class="eyebrow">03</span><strong>Commercial changes</strong><p>Follow quantity changes, price adjustments and renewal decisions.</p></li><li><span class="eyebrow">04</span><strong>Invoice schedule</strong><p>Keep the commercial basis for invoicing available to your accounting process.</p></li></ol></section>

<section class="context-section"><div class="container"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Independently useful. Better together.</p><h2>CRM knows the opportunity.<br />ERP knows the invoice.<br /><em>Revenue knows the relationship.</em></h2><p>Serga Revenue complements CRM and ERP. Start with the commercial records you need, and connect your existing systems where useful.</p></div><div class="capability-grid"><article><h3>Independently useful</h3><p>Use Revenue for software licenses, maintenance, equipment subscriptions or recurring services without Services, Contracts or Leasing.</p></article><article><h3>Alongside CRM & ERP</h3><p>Keep opportunity management and accounting in their respective systems. Connect the commercial context through available integrations.</p></article><article><h3>Better together, when relevant</h3><p>An Internet order in Services can relate to a subscription in Revenue. Contracts can add agreement context. Both connections are optional.</p></article></div></div></section>

<section class="final-cta"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Make the connection</p><h2>Keep recurring business<br /><em>in view.</em></h2><a class="button button-light" href="/contact">Book a demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><span class="cta-tagline">Your gateway to services</span></div></section>
